lizedStatus":"suspicious","score":86,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":28,"checkedAt":1789175407041},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a coherent resume-assistant prompt package, with no hidden execution or persistence, but users should handle resume data and HTML exports carefully.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Processing resumes and job descriptions is necessary for the skill, but that data can contain sensitive personal information; external API examples are placeholders rather than publisher-controlled endpoints.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No installer, executable code, dependency setup, credential request, or privileged install behavior was found; integration examples register a local skill path and manifest.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Natural-language routing includes some broad phrases such as convert, save, and review, but the system prompt also says to ask for clarification when intent is unclear.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No memory writes, background workers, scheduled tasks, tool replacement, credential/session access, or privilege escalation instructions were found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The declared purpose matches the artifacts: prompts and templates support resume polishing, job customization, scoring, and export.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, assume resume content may be processed by your chosen agent or LLM provider and redact unnecessary personal details. Prefer explicit /resume commands for sensitive documents, confirm before exporting files, and ensure any HTML export implementation escapes user fields and blocks unsafe link schemes.","findings":"[P2] expected: The flagged HTML comments in template files are visible template metadata such as style, font, color, and notes; they do not contain hidden agent-control instructions.\n[SQP-1] expected: Broad routing examples are partly expected for a conversational resume skill, but integrators should require resume-specific context or confirmation before export or transformation actions.\n[SQP-2] expected: The skill necessarily asks users to provide resume and job-description content; the main gap is missing privacy guidance, not evidence of covert collection.\n[E1] expected: The curl examples use a placeholder domain, your-agent-api.com, to show how an integrator might call its own agent API; no hardcoded exfiltration destination was found.\n[SQP-3] expected: English and Chinese defaults appear to be stated language-support limits for the skill rather than an unsafe locale override.\n[T09] unexpected: The HTML export template contains raw placeholders in text, class, and href contexts; this is not malicious by itself, but consuming implementations should escape fields and validate URLs before producing HTML or PDF output.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789175407041}}}}}